NATIONAT ASSEM BLY SECRETARIAT
ORDERS OF THE DAY
for the meeting of the National Assembly to be held on Friday, the 17th January, 2025 at
11.00 a.m.t. Tilowot, Hodith, Noot and national anthem.QUESTIONS
2. Questions entered in a separate list to be asked and answers given.
CALLING ATTEN
TION NOTICE
3. MS. ASTYA NAZ TANOLI MS. NUZHAT SADrqMs. ZAHRA WADOOD FATEMI MS. SHAISTA KHAN to invite attention of theMinister for Parliamentary Affairs to a matter of urgent public importance regardingpersistent gender gap between male and female voters, which continues to effectwomen's full participation in the electoral process, causing grave concern amongst thepu blic.MOTION
4. SENATOR MOHAMMAD ISHAq DAR, Deputy Prime Minister / Minister for ForeignAffairs to move under rule 288 of the Rules of Procedure and Conduct of Business in theNational Assembly, 2007 that the requirement of sub-rule (2) of rule 123 of the said rules besuspended in order to take into consideration the Biological and Toxin Weapons Convention(lm plementatio n) Bill, 2024.LEGISLATIVE BUSINESS
5. SENATOR MOHAMMAD TSHAQ DAR, Deputy Prime Minister / Minister for ForeignAffairs to move that the Bill to give effect to the Convention on the Prohibition of theDevelopment, Production and Stockpiling of Bacteriological (Biological) and Toxin Weaponsand on their Destruction, t972 [The Biological and Toxin Weapons Convention(lmplementatio nl Bill, 202a1, as reported by the Standing Committee, be taken intoconsideration at once.
6. SENATOR MOHAMMAD ISHAq DAR, Deputy Prime Minister / Minlster for ForeignAffairs to move that the Bill to give effect to the Convention on the Prohibition of theDevelopment, Production and Stockpiling of Bacteriological (Biological) and Toxin Weaponsand on their Destruction, 1972 [The Biological and Toxin Weapons Convention(lmplementatio nl Bill, 20241, be passed.
PRESENTATION OF REPORTS O
F THE STANDING COMMITTEE
7, CH. MAHMOOD BASHIR VIRK, Chairman Standing Committee on Law and Justice tomove that delay in presentation of report of the Standing Committee on the Bill further toamend the Civil Courts Ordinance, 1962 [The Civil Courts (Amendment) B:il,2024], till today becondoned.

