8. CH. MAHMOOD EASHIR VIRK, Chairman Standing Committee on Law and Justice topresent report of the Standing Committee on the Bill further to amend the Civil CourtsOrdinance, 1962 [The Civil Courts (Amendment) Btl,2O24l.
9, RAJA KHURRAM SHAHZAD NAWAZ, Chairman Standing Committee on lnterior to movethat delay in presentation of report of the Standing Committee on the Bill further to amendthe Pakistan Coast Guards Act, 1973 [The Pakistan Coast Guards (Amendment) Bill, 2024], tilltoday be condoned.
10, RAJA KHURRAM SHAHZAD NAWAZ, Chairman Standing Committee on lnterior topresent report of the Standing Committee on the Bill further to amend the Pakistan CoastGuards Act, 1973 [The Pakistan Coast Guards (Amendment) 9il,2024).
!7. RAJA KHURRAM SHAHZAD NAWAZ, Chairman Standing Committee on lnterior to movethat delay in presentation of report of the Standing Committee on the Bill further to amendthe Pakistan Citizenship Act, 1951 [The Pakistan Citizenship (Amendment) 9il,2024], till todaybe condoned.
72. RAJA KHURRAM SHAHZAD NAWAZ, Chairman Standing Committee on lnterior topresent report of the Standing Committee on the Bill further to amend the PakistanCitizenship Act, 1951 [The Pakistan Citizenship (Amendment) 8t1,2024].
13. MS. ALIYA KAMRAN to invite attention of the Minister for NationalHealth Services, Regulations and Coordination to a matter of urgent public importanceregarding shortage of medical equipment, including essential items like ventilators, testingmachines and GeneXpert systems, in PIMS, lslamabad, the Federal Government Polyclinic,lslamabad and other federally administered hospitals, causing grave concern amongst thepublic.
TAHIR HUSSAINSecretary General
CALLING ATTENTION NOTICE
lslamabad, the16th Januarv, 2025

